{
  "id" : "ct_sonaveil",
  "title" : "Sonaveil Guide",
  "description" : "A warm guide to celebrating Sona's Veil - the alta cold solstice holiday! ^gray;(Unlocks holiday recipes)^reset;",
  "longdescription" : "This guide covers Sonaveil traditions from building snowaltas to baking the perfect holiday pie, and everything in between - scarves, lights, snow fights, warm drinks, and most importantly, gathering with your sisters for warmth and joy!",
  "altaDescription" : "Makes me want to wrap up in blankets and celebrate right now! So cozy~",
  "icon" : "ebook/enchanted.png",
  "species" : "alta",
  "contentPages" : [
    "^#b0e0fc;Sonaveil Celebration Guide^reset;\n\nA warm holiday during the coldest times!\n\nSona's Veil is our cold solstice celebration - a time to gather, stay warm, and enjoy the beauty of the cold season together! This guide will help you celebrate properly~",
    "^#60c0fc;When to Celebrate^reset;\n\nSonaveil happens during cold seasons around the cold solstice on ^#2080f0;alterash prime^reset; planets. The exact timing varies by planet, but it always coincides with the coldest, darkest time of year!\n\nThe celebration period usually lasts several weeks around the solstice.",
    "^#ff8080;Stay Warm Together^reset;\n\nThe holiday's core message is simple: stay warm together when it's cold outside! This means both literal warmth and emotional warmth through gathering with your sisters.\n\nWrap up in warm blankets, wear layers, and most importantly - huddle together for warmth and comfort~",
    "^#60c0fc;Warm Scarves^reset;\n\nSpecial blue scarves are given out by local outposts during Sonaveil! Though some altas prefer to knit their own - these warm cotton clothes have become the symbol of the holiday.\n\nWearing your scarf shows you're celebrating, and they're perfect for staying cozy during outdoor activities like building snowaltas!",
    "^#ffd080;String Lights & Decorations^reset;\n\nHang colorful string lights everywhere! They brighten the long dark nights and create such a warm, festive atmosphere.\n\nWall scarves and fabric hangings add color and coziness to indoor spaces. The warm reds, yellows, and whites contrast beautifully with the cold blue snow outside!",
    "^#ffffff;Snowaltas^reset;\n\nBuilding snowaltas is one of our favorite traditions! These are alta-shaped snow statues made from:\n\n- Packed snow for the body\n- Crystals for decorative accents\n- Ayaka branches for arms\n- Fruit for the nose\n- Scarves, hats, lights for decoration\n\nThey're so cute standing in the snow!",
    "^#80ffff;Snow Activities^reset;\n\nSonaveil isn't just about staying inside! You can:\n\n- Building snowaltas together\n- Snow fights (snowball cannons make this easy!)\n- Making snow drawings\n- Sledding down hills\n- Walking through fresh snowfall\n\nJust don't forget your warm scarf! It's cold out there~",
    "^#ff8080;Hot Drinks^reset;\n\nStaying warm means drinking warm! Traditional Sonaveil beverages include:\n\n- Hot tonna yaavi milk - sweet and creamy!\n- Warm gheamont tea - gentle and soothing\n- Hot sona milk - made from heated sonava juice\n- Spiced aya punch - festive and warming\n\nServe them in your favorite mug while sitting by the lights~",
    "^#ffb080;Sonaveil Pie^reset;\n\nThe quintessential Sonaveil dish! Made from:\n\n- Cooked gils\n- Sonasweets\n- Koywa dough crust\n- Warming spices\n- Tonna milk butter\n\nThe pie keeps its warmth for hours - some say it needs holiday spirit to bake properly! Every city has their own recipe variation~",
    "^#ffa8e8;Sona's Embrace^reset;\n\nThe perfect Sonaveil pie is called Sona's Embrace:\n\n- Golden-perfect flaky crust\n- Perfectly balanced sweet-spice filling\n- Rich smooth tonna butter\n- Magical lasting warmth\n\nThese are made with genuine love and holiday spirit. Sharing one is a deep expression of sisterly care!",
    "^#ffffff;Other Holiday Foods^reset;\n\nMore delicious Sonaveil treats:\n\n- Sonasweets - baked sonava fruit candies\n- Sona's cake - layered pancakey cake\n- Holiday cookies with warm spices\n- Candied gil slices\n- Roasted tsay with butter\n\nAll perfect for sharing during gatherings!",
    "^#ffd080;Holiday Spirit^reset;\n\nDuring Sonaveil, you might receive gifts of Holiday Spirit - symbolic tokens representing the season's joy and community warmth!\n\nThese little items carry the festive atmosphere with them. Some say they're made from concentrated celebration energy itself!",
    "^#ffffff;Warm Clothing^reset;\n\nDress for the season! Popular Sonaveil attire:\n\n- Warm sweaters and layers\n- The traditional blue scarves\n- Cozy hats and mittens\n- Thick socks and warm boots\n- Festive holiday dresses for indoor parties\n\nStaying warm is staying true to the holiday spirit!",
    "^#ffa8e8;The True Meaning^reset;\n\nAt its heart, Sonaveil celebrates finding warmth - both physical and emotional - during the coldest, darkest time of year.\n\nIt's about gathering with those you love, sharing food and comfort, and reminding each other that together, we can weather any winter.\n\nStay warm, stay together, and happy Sona's Veil!"
  ],
